  "instruction": "Which 2007 Rock and Roll hall of fame inductee had the longest-charting song on the Billboard Hot 100 prior to January 2024? Name the artist and song.",
  "answer": "Now I have complete data for all five 2007 inductees. Let me compile the findings:\n\n## Summary of Longest-Charting Songs by 2007 Inductees\n\n| Inductee | Longest-Charting Song | Weeks on Hot 100 (pre-Jan 2024) |\n|----------|----------------------|----------------------------------|\n| Grandmaster Flash & the Furious Five | \"The Message\" | 7 weeks |\n| **The Ronettes** | **\"Sleigh Ride\"** | **~30–35 weeks** (39 total through 2025-26) |\n| Patti Smith | \"Because the Night\" | 18 weeks |\n| Van Halen | \"Jump\" | 21 weeks |\n| R.E.M. | \"Losing My Religion\" | 21 weeks |\n\n**The Ronettes' \"Sleigh Ride\" is the clear winner.** Even by the January 2024 cutoff, it had accumulated approximately 30–35 weeks on the Hot 100 (first entering December 2018, re-entering each holiday season, peaking at #8 on December 23, 2023), far exceeding the next closest at 21 weeks.\n\n## Sources\n\n1. **2007 Inductee List** — Rock & Roll Hall of Fame official site & Wikipedia: https://rockhall.com/inductees/classes/2007 / https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Rock_and_Roll_Hall_of_Fame_inductees\n2. **Grandmaster Flash & the Furious Five — \"The Message\" (7 weeks)** — Music Charts Archive: http://musicchartsarchive.com/singles/grandmaster-flash-and-the-furious-five/the-message\n3. **The Ronettes — \"Sleigh Ride\" (39 weeks total, ~30–35 by Jan 2024)** — ELPEE.jp Billboard Database: https://elpee.jp/artist/The%20Ronettes / https://elpee.jp/single/Sleigh%20Ride/The%20Ronettes/\n4. **Patti Smith — \"Because the Night\" (18 weeks)** — Music Charts Archive: https://musicchartsarchive.com/singles/patti-smith/because-the-night\n5. **Van Halen — \"Jump\" (21 weeks)** — ELPEE.jp Billboard Database: https://elpee.jp/single/Jump/Van%20Halen\n6. **R.E.M. — \"Losing My Religion\" (21 weeks)** — ELPEE.jp Billboard Database: https://elpee.jp/artist/R.E.M.",
